<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Didata active, special trades lift volumes.</title>
<headline>Didata active, special trades lift volumes.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electronics firm Dimension Data shares rose on Thursday after a foreign sale of 2.3 million shares and a bookover, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a lot of interest in the share. Yesterday it also traded in huge volumes,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>The share was steady at 18.25 rand in a volume of four million shares valued at nearly 86 million rand.</p>
<p>Dealers said a foreign sale of 2.3 million shares and a bookover of 800,000 shares boosted volumes.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482 1003</p>
